From: MilkFlint <milkflint@local>
Subject: [PATCH] mt7981b: restore gbe_led0/1 pinmux nodes

OpenWrt board DTS files (e.g. iptime AX3000M, TOTOLINK X6000R) reference
&gbe_led0_pins / &gbe_led1_pins. The 6.18 port of 117-complete-mt7981b-dtsi
dropped those labels from the SoC dtsi, so image DTB builds fail.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7981b.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7981b.dtsi
@@ -352,6 +352,20 @@
 					drive-strength = <MTK_DRIVE_4mA>;
 				};
 			};
+
+			gbe_led0_pins: gbe-led0-pins {
+				mux {
+					function = "led";
+					groups = "gbe_led0";
+				};
+			};
+
+			gbe_led1_pins: gbe-led1-pins {
+				mux {
+					function = "led";
+					groups = "gbe_led1";
+				};
+			};
 		};
 
 		efuse@11f20000 {
